TOGGLE                                   *kkiyama117-nvim-commands-background*

==============================================================================
Background color toggle                           *kkiyama117-nvim-background*

TODO: this is AI-generated, and I think this contents is not `Commands` of
nvim

`vimrc.utils` provides functions to toggle the background color between
`NONE` (transparent) and the colorscheme default background color.

The background of the following highlight groups is toggled: >
	Normal		NormalNC	SignColumn	SignColumnSB
	LineNr		LineNrAbove	LineNrBelow	CursorLineNr
	EndOfBuffer	FoldColumn	Folded		FloatBorder
	NormalFloat	MsgArea
<

When the transparency is enabled, the original background colors of the
groups are saved, and they are restored when the transparency is disabled.

If the colorscheme is transparent by default, the default background color
of the colorscheme is resolved and used instead:
- catppuccin: `palette.base`
- tokyonight: `colors.bg`
- nightfox:   `palette.bg1` (default background; `bg0` is for statusline
  and floats)

For other colorschemes, the colorscheme is re-sourced to restore its
defaults.

Functions: >
	require('vimrc.utils').toggle_background()
	require('vimrc.utils').background_transparent()
	require('vimrc.utils').background_opaque()
	require('vimrc.utils').is_background_transparent()
<

Mapping: >
	[TOGGLE]b	Toggle the background transparency
<

